            <ArticleTitle>Referred shoulder pain preceding abdominal pain in a teenage girl with gastric perforation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>807-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Referred shoulder pain is an important yet potentially distracting sign of serious intra-abdominal illness. A case is presented wherein shoulder pain preceded by several hours the onset of abdominal pain in a teenage girl with gastric perforation. The range of causes of gastric perforation and the pathophysiology of referred shoulder pain are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
